Free MuJoCo's GL resources on the render thread when the viewer closes.
 
The GLFW window and its GL context are created on the UI thread, but Simulate
(and its GlfwAdapter) is destroyed later by ~MujocoSimulation on another thread.
~GlfwAdapter calls mjr_freeContext there, with no GL context current, and the
GL driver segfaults (seen in libGLdispatch on NVIDIA) on every shutdown with the
viewer. Freeing the context right after RenderLoop() returns, while it is still
current, leaves nothing for the later call to delete (mjr_freeContext only
issues GL calls for non-zero handles and resets the context).
 
--- a/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp
+++ b/src/mujoco_simulation.cpp
@@ -625,6 +625,9 @@
       // Blocks until terminated
       RCLCPP_INFO(get_logger(), "Starting the MuJoCo rendering thread...");
       sim_->RenderLoop();
+      // The GL context is current on this thread only; free MuJoCo's GL
+      // resources here rather than in ~GlfwAdapter on the destroying thread.
+      mjr_freeContext(&sim_->platform_ui->mjr_context());
 
       if (detail::handle_render_loop_exit(sim_->exitrequest, explicit_shutdown_requested_,
                                           node_->get_node_base_interface()->get_context()))
